§ `s 7(2), (3) -- k084: Jake's time to claim against Graham's estate (grant HYPOTHETICALLY 14 October 2052)`

#ASSERT `What is the last day I can apply without leave` (Date 14 10 2052) EQUALS (Date 14 4 2053)

#ASSERT `Is my application in time` (Date 14 10 2052) (Date 1 3 2053) FALSE EQUALS `in time: made within 6 months from the grant (s 7(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` (Date 14 10 2052) (Date 15 4 2053) FALSE EQUALS `out of time: it will not be heard unless the Court is satisfied the justice of the case requires leave, which I may seek at any time (s 7(2)(b), (3))`
#ASSERT `Is my application in time` (Date 14 10 2052) (Date 15 4 2053) TRUE EQUALS `out of time, but it will be heard: the Court has given leave to file out of time (s 7(2)(b))`

§ `s 6(1), (3) -- can the Court order provision for me (k084 Jake; d085 nobody applies)`

#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `yes: I am a person by whom an application may be made (s 7(1))` TRUE `in time: made within 6 months from the grant (s 7(2)(a))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Court may order such provision for me as it thinks fit, as a lump sum or a periodical or other payment, with conditions (s 6(1), (3), (4))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `yes: I am a person by whom an application may be made (s 7(1))` TRUE `in time: made within 6 months from the grant (s 7(2)(a))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no order: the Court is not of the opinion that adequate provision was not made for my proper maintenance, support, education or advancement in life (s 6(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `yes: I am a person by whom an application may be made (s 7(1))` FALSE `in time: made within 6 months from the grant (s 7(2)(a))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no order: no application has been made by me or on my behalf (s 6(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `no: I am not in any class that section 7(1) names` TRUE `in time: made within 6 months from the grant (s 7(2)(a))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no order: I am not a person who may apply (s 7(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `yes: I am a person by whom an application may be made (s 7(1))` TRUE `out of time: it will not be heard unless the Court is satisfied the justice of the case requires leave, which I may seek at any time (s 7(2)(b), (3))` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no order: my application will not be heard, being out of time without leave (s 7(2))`
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me` `yes: I am a person by whom an application may be made (s 7(1))` TRUE `out of time, but it will be heard: the Court has given leave to file out of time (s 7(2)(b))` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no order: the Court refuses because of my character or conduct, or on another ground it thinks sufficient (s 6(3))`

